WEBVTT

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.850
Hokorimamire no bonnet

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:23.250
yubi de kyou o kizamu

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.620
Toori ame ga sugiru koro

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.560
ai no you ni kieta

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:36.630
Kokoro no naka nakusenu mono aru Kara

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:43.140
Mienai tsubasa habatakase

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:50.170
Koredemo katto fuku kaze ni mukaiuchi

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:57.420
Yuruginai kimochi de tachimukatteku no sa, go!

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:04.330
Sunabokori mau yakusoku no basho e

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:10.330
oretachi wa hashiritsuzukete yuku

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:13.460
Konya koso

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.970
Koete yaru

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:24.520
Ano saki made

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:37.780
Episode 5     NEVER CHANGE

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.620
All set!

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:42.360
Sweet! I'm starving!

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.920
Okay, shall we get started?

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:47.870
Let's go over things one more time.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:49.070
Just listen to me while you're eating, all right?

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:50.310
Well, thanks for the food!

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.840
If we say this bacon represents where we are now,

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.280
then this is Graceland.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:59.410
Getting there would take us about
twenty-one days at an ordinary cruise.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.580
Which means, by the time we got there,

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:06.780
Bruce's legacy would have already vanished
into the oblivion of space.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:10.850
So that means our only choice
is to take a warp gate, right?

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:15.930
The closest gate facility is Big Pink
in the Woody system.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:20.200
From there, we'll come out the Graceland gate,
and make the trip in one straight shot.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.830
The time factor makes that our only choice.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.270
Guess so.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:25.800
Fime vy me!

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:27.880
Naturally, they'll probably conduct an inspection.

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:31.480
And it's possible the Guild has
them under its thumb too.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:32.780
The Guild?

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:36.280
Each system puts on its own
little decorative facade,

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:37.950
but beneath the surface they're all scum.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.920
Which is why they're friggin' in
with the Guild on everything.

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:42.260
Huh...

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:44.850
Hey, this stuffs great!

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:49.460
Oh, that's a new item we've had on the menu
at the Pirate Hideout since last month!

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:50.790
Let me try.

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:55.770
Damn, this is good!

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.570
You sure know how to cook, Franca!

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:00.070
You think so?

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.070
Fabulous!

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.100
Yep!

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:09.080
Even if we make it to Graceland,

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.620
next we'll have our encounter with
Gigabanks waiting for us,

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:14.590
and in the middle of a war no less.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.050
We've got a long way to go, but not much time.

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.560
This ship stands out just a bit too.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.830
Before we're found by the enemy, 
let's jump straight into the enemy's belly.

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:26.730
I'll set out the bait we need to make 'em bite.
I've got just the thing.

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:30.270
Send a message a thousand space kilometers
out towards Big Pink:

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.970
"The Persian Kitty wants to eat
some fall salmon."

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:36.180
All right! Guess I'll stuff my face and
then get down to business!

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.980
Franca, is there any more of this?

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:40.420
Yeah, there is. Shall I get you seconds?

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.250
Nah, that's all right. I'll get it myself.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.580
There's still some of this left too.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.390
Oh! Thank you!

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:52.990
Whoa, whoa, WHOA!

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:54.260
Oh, sorry!

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.880
<i>At 6:00 PM Geteldova local time,</i>

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:02.360
<i>the new generation photonic bomb "Jupiter"
was sent off with an array of escort vessels.</i>

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:07.310
<i>The date, time and point at which the bomb
will be dropped have not been revealed,</i>

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:10.640
<i>but the convoy appears to be heading
for the Moonwalk's Fussa Gate.</i>

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.770
All right then...

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.760
Let's have a few answers from you, shall we?

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.570
Why did Marciano start a rebellion?

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:38.340
Given the Guild's present situation
and her place within the Guild,

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.010
I can't come up with any reason
that she'd do such a thing.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.750
Mother has her own intentions.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.310
What intentions?

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:49.420
We Twelve Sisters only carry out Mother's orders.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:51.980
What will she accomplish by taking over the Guild?

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:54.090
While you eat that sushi,

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:58.320
do you have a particular reason in mind
for swallowing each and every piece?

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:06.430
Okay, then what has Marciano ordered you to do?

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:07.770
Could you tell me that?

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:10.970
No?

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.970
Well, I don't see why not.

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:16.680
The instructions Mother has given me
are to go to Ku-Rong

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:21.140
and take both Mister and a little girl
named Franca alive.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:25.180
And to then get them to spit out
the location of the treasure.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.560
Mister and Franca...

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:29.820
Treasure?

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:31.660
What could that be about?

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:35.100
Why do you want to know so badly anyhow?

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.900
Why? Well, because it's my job to.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.130
That's right.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:42.500
Angelica has been doggedly pursuing
Mister since she became a detective.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.410
She's been on his tail for four years straight!

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:44.170
Thank you.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.700
Well, hats off to you, Honey.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.210
None of it makes any sense.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.010
A treasure... Franca...

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:53.910
And what's the connection between Mister
and Marciano in the first place?

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.050
Where the heck is Mister trying to go?

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:58.990
I do know where they're headed.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:00.020
Huh?!

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:01.320
You know'?!

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:04.990
Yeah, I do know where they're headed.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:07.020
Hey, Mister!

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:12.600
Do you think there's a chance the war will just come
to a halt and that bomb won't be dropped?

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.440
Well, now...

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.670
The war itself all started from a
stupid little misunderstanding

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:20.770
between the Federation government
and Graceland's government.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:25.200
This whole war is nothing but an
idiotic battle of egos.

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:29.180
Then you mean it's all in the hands of
the top brass on either side?

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:33.120
Oh, man, that's the worst...

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:35.390
I'll go check on the autopilot real quick.

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:36.290
Okay.

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:39.160
How about you go do a little maintenance yourself?

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:40.290
Shaddup!

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:43.900
Don't you have any preparations to get in order
for breaking into Gigabanks?

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.400
Don't get the wrong idea here.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:50.360
I only came along to see whether this guy's really
man enough to be able to take Bruce's inheritance.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:52.440
Oh, is that right?

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:53.530
Pah!

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:02.420
Hey, what's the deal?

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.290
Whatcha doing all alone here?

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.190
Oh, nothing.

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:10.020
So tell me, what are you going to do
after this job's done?

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:11.590
What am I going to do?

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:13.660
Good question!

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:17.130
I haven't really given the future much thought.

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:18.730
What are you gonna do, Franca?

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:20.800
Will you go back to the Pirate Hideout?

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:22.740
You and Mister could both...

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:26.170
Yeah, I wonder what he'll do?

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:29.740
He was with me for my father's legacy.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:33.700
That's why I'll only be with him for five more days.

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:35.820
Then that'll be it.

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.990
Listen, it's not like that!

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:41.360
That's not the reason Mister is with you!

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.520
He said the same thing himself.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.520
But I don't know what the truth is.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:50.600
I don't think that's the case,
but then again it could happen.

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:54.870
That's why... That's why I couldn't
hand over the pendant.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:57.340
If I had, then...

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:59.470
there wouldn't have been any more need for me.

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:01.440
That's what I thought.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.810
Franca...

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:09.380
I wonder if I'll be on my own again once this is over?

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:12.510
Katana...

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:17.020
Don't tell anyone what I just said.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.960
Yeah, all right.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.800
So we hooked 'em?!

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:29.040
This is Persian Kitty, Persian Kitty here.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:31.100
Do you have any tasty fall salmon?

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:36.170
We have 1,200 of them here. We have 1,200 here.

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:37.610
Roger!

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:39.770
Request guidance data.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:42.610
Looks like this will go smoothly!

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.890
You got everything set?

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:18.110
Hi! Nice to meet ya, Captain!

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.490
What an incredibly splendid ship you've got here!

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:23.510
I am honored to make your acquaintance.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:31.730
These vintage Hawaiian shins are 150 years old.

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:34.700
They're in super-super-duper-mint condition.
Not a single spot on 'em!

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:37.070
Whaddya say? Yours for a mere 10,000!

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:38.110
Ten thousand?

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.210
Okay, that's good.

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:42.540
Touching the merchandise is off-limits, sir!
You can touch only after you've made your purchase!

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:45.950
Well, how about it?
That's super cheap, wouldn't you say?

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:49.450
If you're heading over to a lady's place after this,
I'd say the yellow would do the trick.

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:52.990
This yellow one is made out of
legendary Kamchatkan thread,

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:55.460
and even we've got only one in stock!

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:56.490
Only one!

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:58.460
See, it's beautiful, isn't it?

00:09:58.460 --> 00:09:59.950
So beautiful!

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:04.730
If yellows no good, we've also got
some nice, manly blue ones.

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:05.970
Right here, we've got some...

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:07.900
No, no, that's all right.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:10.200
More importantly, where's the stuff?

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:11.010
Huh?

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.340
Persia! Persia, man!

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:17.080
Sheesh, the girls don't dig hasty guys, y'know!

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:20.410
In all things, the proper process is most important.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:23.020
Hey, verify it's for real!

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:23.980
Uh, right!

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:27.420
Well?

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:29.920
It's 99.99% pure.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:31.230
This is very pure stuff!

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.630
What do you say?

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:34.160
We'll take it, of course!

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:36.900
Thank ya very much!

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:40.130
You've made a swell purchase, Captain.

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:43.600
By the way, where's this ship headed from here?

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:46.740
Our plan is to go to Fussa via Big Pink.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:50.510
I don't suppose we could go along with you?

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:54.120
If it would be any trouble for you, then let's just
pretend we never had this conversation.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.450
Look, I don't want any trouble...

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:58.490
Thank ya very much!

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:02.590
My, oh my, export restrictions on vintage items
have become so strict!

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:04.520
Yeah, terrible.

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:08.660
Would you like one too, First Officer?

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.830
Ah, no, I...

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:14.440
Here, what about this color?
I think it suits you perfectly!

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:15.440
Whoa, hold on!

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:18.510
Nah, this is what a stylin' guy like you needs!

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:22.100
If it's those two, give 'em away for a hundred...
Nah, make that nintey!

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:25.880
All right, all right. You win. I'll take them both.

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:27.720
Thank you kindly!

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:30.020
Now, where was my wallet...

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:31.750
Here, let me hold that for you.

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:32.910
Oh, thanks.

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:50.970
Docking sequence currently underway.

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:53.340
Now commencing approach.

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:55.810
Okay, move in at low speed.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:58.310
All hands, stand by in your designated positions.

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:00.310
Roger. Moving in at low speed.

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:04.420
Vessel number B9-664582,
you have clearance to dock.

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:07.020
Please proceed on course to Gate 5.

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:08.180
I repeat...

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:12.290
I'm counting on you, man.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.730
Please let this work.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:20.830
Gate cleared. Now entering scanning block.

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:28.430
Commencing scan of vessel number B9-664582.

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:30.910
Please maintain present speed.

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:41.390
This is the control room.

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:46.060
Scan of vessel number B9-664582 is now complete.

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:51.000
Please follow guidance signal 75-8,
and proceed to Gate N-6.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:54.960
Following arrival, all passengers must
proceed through immigrations.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.630
What's the deal with the getup?

00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:25.600
I just wanted to try it for once.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.570
Well, it sure looks lousy!

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.640
Are you kidding? It's totally cool!

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.370
You're just too old.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:34.010
Ain't that right, Franca?

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:35.440
Eh, heh heh...

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:38.430
Well, I think it's pretty damn sweet.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:48.290
Well, now. So far, so good.

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:53.630
And so we sit back to enjoy some
tea or whatever, but in fact...

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:57.360
Sure enough, the Graceland gate is closed.

00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:59.970
Well, now, this is the place, is it?

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:03.500
The gate itself is operating,
even if the entrance is closed,

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:05.670
so busting our way through is always an option.

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:10.080
I'll bet it was naive, wishful thinking like that
that caused your screw-up on Sandvil too, huh?

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:12.940
Shut the hell up!
Cripes, it's always something with you!

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.540
You do have a plan, right?

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:18.680
Okay, how about I explain?

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:24.320
The gate leading to Graceland is this way.
This is how it's set up.

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:28.700
Odds are that gate is being operated remotely
from the control tower.

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:32.530
First, we need to cut this link. Then we'll open
the gate manually and push on through.

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:33.830
Whoa, slow down.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:37.140
How are we supposed to cut off the remote link
without any sort of diagram or blueprint?

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:38.910
Oh, I've got your blueprints.

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:41.210
When we went to the Pirate Hideout
back on Ku-Rong,

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:42.940
I made sure to ask the guys there for 'em.

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:45.410
You're one good planner.

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:50.520
Please wait up, Angelica!

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:55.490
Don't be so upset!

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.830
I have every reason to be upset!

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.030
We go to the guard room,

00:14:59.030 --> 00:15:01.520
and they tell us we need to go to
the Traffic Safety Department.

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.160
We go to the Traffic Safety Department,

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:05.370
and they start giving us crap over Section 1
versus Section 2 responsibilities!

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:08.530
We don't have a moment to spare, and the
officials here are a bunch of buffoons!

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:10.870
Coulda sworn you're an official yourself.

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:21.210
Whoa, stop it, you idiot! Cut it out, dammit! Whoa!

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:16.610
Take it easy, Angelica!

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:21.210
That's technically impounded evidence, so you've got to be careful with it!

00:15:23.550 --> 00:15:28.010
I'm thinking Miss Angelica there has got an antenna
tuned to your frequency or something.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:29.490
She's something.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:32.720
Now we really can't afford to sit around. Let's go.

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:42.660
What's the matter, Franca?

00:15:43.970 --> 00:15:47.000
What a totally beautiful place...

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:51.370
I wonder if that's what Graceland used to be like?

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.380
Aquaria, huh?

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:57.950
"Never change."
Same now as it will be for eternity.

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:00.720
Have you ever been to this place?

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:04.260
Nope, it's too dazzling a place for the likes of us.

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:05.450
Ah...

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.630
Huh? What's up?

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:13.900
Hey, what's the deal?

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:16.170
Wait there a sec.

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:18.470
Hey, got a second there?

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:20.770
Yes, sir, welcome. What can I do for you?

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:25.650
Well, you see, one of my friends took a liking
to that poster you've got hanging out front.

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:27.150
Think I could have one?

00:16:27.150 --> 00:16:29.350
Uh, I don't think we can do that...

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:30.750
No deal?

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:32.220
I'm afraid there's not much I can do about it.

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:37.080
Then how about if I sign up for this trip?
It'd be all right then, wouldn't it?

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:38.390
Well, yes...

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:39.590
All right!

00:16:39.590 --> 00:16:42.360
Make that five tickets from Ku-Rong to Aquaria!

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:46.370
Let's all go together! To celebrate
the conquest of Graceland!

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:47.870
Sounds good to me!

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:50.240
Hey, you sure you can afford that?

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:53.670
C'mon, don't be such a tight-ass.
It'll only make you older!

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:55.640
You just mind your own business.

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:00.710
We'll split into three groups.

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:04.550
One will take the Coyote here from
the Guild ship to the gate.

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:09.790
The next group will cut off the control tower's link.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:14.190
Damn it! For me to end up with this job.

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:17.960
Then the third group will open
the gate to Graceland!

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:31.750
Chief!

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:36.420
The identification code for Guild Leader Marciano's
ship has come up on the incoming vessel list.

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:39.020
I have received no such word.

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:41.790
They are requesting docking and port entry lists.

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.390
How shall I proceed?

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:44.830
Do as they say.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:45.830
But, sir...

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:46.950
Just do it.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:49.830
Don't think, just do.

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:53.290
Do you want to get this whole terminal blown away?

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:05.040
Eternity, huh?

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:09.250
Katana and Swamp, once you've
taken off with the Coyote,

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:12.990
come out of the mooring docks and head
straight for the Graceland gate.

00:18:12.990 --> 00:18:14.860
Be quick, but don't rush it.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:16.920
If you're noticed...

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:19.090
If you're noticed then force your way through!

00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:21.490
That's what you're best at, right?

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:27.330
Bishop, when you're done cutting off the remote
control link, you head for the Graceland gate too.

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:30.900
Easy enough for him to say! Jeez!

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:33.410
If security picks up a problem with
something that's not in use,

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:35.240
then it's up to the officials
to take care of it.

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:36.680
Shouldn't be a problem for us.

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:40.910
Chief! The Graceland gate is
throwing an error code!

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:42.750
Another malfunction?

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:43.750
How shall I proceed?

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:45.450
It won't be in use for a while anyway.

00:18:45.450 --> 00:18:47.820
Contact the repair center or whoever.

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:52.720
Okay, let's go!

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:55.200
This is Katana...

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:57.060
And Swamp!

00:18:57.060 --> 00:19:00.500
We haven't run into any problems yet,
and we're headed towards the gate now.

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:05.870
Bishop the Great speaking.
Not like I'd ever screw up.

00:19:05.870 --> 00:19:07.440
That's all, signing off.

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:08.810
Whoa...

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:09.780
This one, right?

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:14.610
Where the hell am I?!

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:22.450
That's what I've been telling you!

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:26.260
You need to set up a guard around
the Graceland gate at once,

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:29.460
and conduct a thorough check of all
vessels that have come in to port.

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:32.600
It's not so simple for me to act
on such a sudden request.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:34.470
You're the one who's in charge here, aren't you?

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:35.540
There's no time to waste!

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:40.630
Though I am in charge, these matters
are not at my sole discretion.

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:47.740
We have entered the docking area.
We are on course towards the Graceland gate.

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:51.120
I have verified the data on the port entry list.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:56.110
Comparing this with personal data, there are
five people who come within a 95% match.

00:19:56.620 --> 00:20:02.100
Send our aircraft out ahead to the Graceland gate,
and see that our soldiers are prepared for landing.

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:08.200
And have the control room forward us the video
feed from all security cameras around the gate.

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:11.440
You all go ahead and take care
of your preparations too.

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:13.500
Yes, Mother.

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:20.210
Canned peaches, canned peaches!

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:22.530
Hurry, hurry!
We can eat these first, right?

00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:35.560
Franca! How's it going over there?

00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:37.660
Fine, I'm just about done.

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:39.830
Okay, it's opening!

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:43.460
We did it!

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:47.570
Where are we going now'?

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:49.380
To the Graceland gate.

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:51.740
Huh? Are you sure it's okay to
go there without asking?

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:55.920
If Mister wants to go to Graceland, then there's
no doubt he's got to go through that gate.

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.750
Well, even a kid could figure out that much.

00:20:58.050 --> 00:21:00.750
Oh, come on, Angelica!

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:03.920
The gate's opened! Now move!

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:05.710
Boss! We've got trouble!

00:21:06.060 --> 00:21:09.220
We've got Guild fighters on our tail!

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:11.690
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:15.430
I don't know where I am!

00:21:17.070 --> 00:21:19.230
Gimme a break...

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:25.700
WHERE THE HELL AM I?!

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:28.570
What are you doing fooling around? Get a move on!

00:21:28.750 --> 00:21:30.050
C'mon, we're gonna hook up with 'em!

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:35.560
There's no way we'll be able to hook up with
you like this! If I slow down, we're dead.

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:36.890
What now'?

00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:53.930
I'm out!

00:21:54.470 --> 00:21:55.670
Where's this?

00:21:56.180 --> 00:21:57.940
Bishop! At two o'clock!

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:15.560
Those bastards have opened fire?

00:22:21.100 --> 00:22:22.870
Are you all set?

00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:25.500
Yes, Mother.

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:44.520
<i>Hoho o tsutawaru</i>

00:22:44.520 --> 00:22:54.840
<i>shizuku doko kara kuru no</i>

00:22:54.840 --> 00:22:58.970
<i>Oshiete...</i>

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:05.110
<i>Makimodosenai</i>

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:12.650
<i>jikan to iu ruuru ni</i>

00:23:12.650 --> 00:23:20.030
<i>munagura tsukanda</i>

00:23:20.490 --> 00:23:24.100
<i>Koko ni aru "omoi" de sae</i>

00:23:24.100 --> 00:23:27.170
<i>usuragu kioku ni</i>

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:34.410
<i>teikou suru keredo</i>

00:23:34.670 --> 00:23:37.910
<i>Kitto koroshi ni kuru</i>

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:44.550
<i>Sugite kita hibi no naka de</i>

00:23:44.550 --> 00:23:53.030
<i>tatta hitotsu shinjirareru</i>

00:23:53.030 --> 00:23:59.370
<i>Koe o karasete naita</i>

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:02.700
<i>Koko e kite</i>

00:24:02.700 --> 00:24:06.370
<i>Soba ni ite</i>

00:24:06.370 --> 00:24:10.000
<i>Nee</i>
